      "content": "I see. You mentioned a sudden activation of metabolic pathways being triggered by environmental cues. Can you go deeper into the specific enzymatic mechanisms involved in that \"hyper-active mode\"? \n\nI'm particularly interested in how the substrate concentration (glucose vs. maltose) triggers this shift in the *Lactobacillus* population. Is there a specific metabolic switch, like certain phosphotransferase systems (PTS), that regulates this transition from steady state to that sudden acidity spike? I really need to understand the biochemistry so I can adjust my feeding ratios to prevent these spikes.",
